2052:    30	**`scripts/dev.mjs` is a hand-rolled process coordinator, not just a script runner.** It exists specifically to avoid orphaned child processes: it validates ports before spawning anything, resolves `tsc`/`vite` binaries directly via `process.execPath` (no shell, no `npx`) to avoid extra shell-spawned layers, tracks children in a `Set`, and on `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` sends `SIGTERM` to all children with a 400ms grace period before `SIGKILL`. Any process this script or the backend spawns in the future (e.g. the Phase 2 Python MLX worker) needs to be registered the same way and torn down within that shutdown path — this has already been audited once (see `docs/audits/phase-2-audit-result-v2.log`, Achado v2-6) for a case where a subprocess needed more than the 400ms force-kill window.
2056:    34	**Voice runtime (Phase 2) lives in `src/backend/voice/`** and is optional at the process level: `voiceRuntime.ts` only constructs the real `MlxWorkerEngine` (spawns `scripts/worker/worker.py`, a persistent Python/MLX process talking NDJSON over stdio) if `.runtime/.venv` and `.runtime/models-manifest.json` exist (i.e. `npm run setup:voice` has run) — otherwise `/api/voice/*` returns a `503` with a PT-BR explanation and the rest of the app keeps working. `sessionManager.ts` enforces one active session at a time with synchronous preemption (a new session immediately supersedes the old one — never makes the user wait out the 10-minute idle timeout), cooperative turn cancellation (never kills/restarts the worker for a normal barge-in — that's reserved for catastrophic failures), and only commits an assistant sentence to the LLM's conversation history after the client confirms it actually finished playing (`POST /api/voice/session/played`) — a turn that gets barge-in'd mid-sentence never makes the model believe it said something the user didn't hear. Test coverage (`src/backend/__tests__/voice.test.ts`) uses `FakeVoiceEngine`/a fake `IVoiceProvider` and never depends on Python/MLX being installed; set `RODRIGO_VOICE_DISABLE=1` when spawning a real server subprocess in a test to skip constructing the real engine regardless of local `.runtime` state.
